  "body": "## What happens\n\nThe release-tier preflight of the v0.23.0 cut ran on main `93fe3cfd0` (Windows, release profile, `--ignored` heavy lanes). Two heavy-lane tests in `camcraft-motion` fail:\n\n1. `crates/motion/tests/adaptive_hsm.rs:468`, `a_small_helix_rectangle_never_crosses_itself`:\n   `assertion left == right failed: one helix per level`, left 2, right 3.\n2. `crates/motion/tests/rotary_adaptive.rs:289`, `the_r62_neck_levels_are_hsm_planned_on_microlift_returns`:\n   `the skin level stays HSM-planned`. The notes show only the levels at radius 5.700 and 5.200.\n\nThe two tests are `#[ignore]`d. The quick and batch gates do not run them.\n\n## Cause\n\nPR #2013 (issue #2004) changed the shared depth ladder. The first level is now one stepdown under Top Z. The old level at Top Z cut air and is gone. This is the intended result of a reviewed PR.\n\nEvidence:\n\n- The rectangle has Top Z 0, Bottom Z -4, Stepdown 2. The ladder is now `[-2, -4]`: two helices, not three.\n- The debug twin `level_links::the_helix_entry_is_one_continuous_descent` was updated by #2013 to two helices (\"-2, -4; #2004: none at Top Z\").\n- The r6.2 bar is r6 at most. The level on the r6.2 stock skin cut air. #2013 removed it and updated the other tests in `rotary_adaptive.rs` (`no level on the r7 skin (#2004)`, the `GOLDEN_RINGS` re-pin). It did not update these two ignored tests.\n\nNo toolpath behaviour is lost. The expectations are stale.\n\n## Fix\n\nUpdate the two expectations to pin the new behaviour with the same strength, on branch `cut/0.23-heavy-lanes` (release cut fix, no PR):\n\n- `adaptive_hsm`: two helices, and each helix lands on -2 and -4.\n- `rotary_adaptive`: no level on the r6.2 skin. The asserts on the 5.7 and 5.2 levels stay.\n\nDone means: the two tests pass in release with `--ignored`, and the two whole test binaries pass with and without `--ignored`.\n",
